verview": "Nancy Mace's retirement leaves this Charleston-area seat open, and the Republican lean of the district gives the GOP a starting edge. Jenny Costa Honeycutt won a contested primary and carries modest resources, while Democrat Nancy Lacore has raised over $2.2 million and is running a healthcare-focused campaign with outside support behind her.\n\nMost expert ratings land at Lean or Likely Republican, though The Economist calls it a Tossup. The two available polls, both Democratic-sponsored, show a race within a few points. Prediction markets give the Republican roughly a 70% chance. The forecast expects a narrow Republican win of about four points, with meaningful uncertainty given the thin and partisan polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2812, "margin": -3.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2869, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3426, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2761, "margin": -4.0}]}